          "chapter": "Matrices",
          "topic": "Matrix multiplication and order",
          "content_type": "explanation",
          "text": "If A has order m × n and B has order n × p, the product AB is defined and has order m × p. Each entry is a row-by-column dot product. Matrix multiplication is generally not commutative: AB need not equal BA, and one product may be defined while the other is not.",
