          "subject": "Mathematics",
          "class": 12,
          "chapter": "Matrices",
          "topic": "Matrix multiplication and order",
          "content_type": "worked_example",
          "text": "Let A = [[1,2],[0,1]] and B = [[2,0],[1,3]]. Then AB = [[4,6],[1,3]], while BA = [[2,4],[1,5]]. Both products exist, but they are not equal.",
