          "topic": "Increasing and decreasing functions",
          "content_type": "explanation",
          "text": "On an interval where a differentiable function has f'(x) > 0, it is increasing; where f'(x) < 0, it is decreasing. Critical points where f'(x) = 0 or is undefined divide the domain into intervals to test. A sign chart for the derivative supports the conclusion on each interval.",
          "reference_id": "adapted-original-mathematics-12",
          "syllabus_reference_id": "cbse-2026-27-mathematics-041",
          "page_start": null,
          "page_end": null,
