          "chapter": "Applications of Derivatives",
          "topic": "Increasing and decreasing functions",
          "content_type": "worked_example",
          "text": "For f(x) = x^2 - 4x, f'(x) = 2x - 4. It is negative for x < 2 and positive for x > 2, so f decreases on (-∞, 2) and increases on (2, ∞).",
