          "concept_id": "math-12-definite-integrals",
          "subject": "Mathematics",
          "class": 12,
          "chapter": "Integrals",
          "topic": "Definite integrals and symmetry",
          "content_type": "worked_example",
          "text": "Because x^2 is even, ∫_-2^2 x^2 dx = 2∫_0^2 x^2 dx = 2[x^3/3]_0^2 = 16/3. The symmetry shortcut applies because f(-x) = f(x).",
          "reference_id": "adapted-original-mathematics-12",
