          "subject": "Mathematics",
          "class": 12,
          "chapter": "Continuity and Differentiability",
          "topic": "Continuity at a point",
          "content_type": "explanation",
          "text": "A function f is continuous at x = a when f(a) is defined, lim(x→a)f(x) exists, and that limit equals f(a). A graph may have a removable hole, jump, or unbounded behavior; each fails at least one part of the condition.",
          "reference_id": "adapted-original-mathematics-12",
          "syllabus_reference_id": "cbse-2026-27-mathematics-041",
          "page_start": null,
          "page_end": null,
