          "subject": "Mathematics",
          "class": 12,
          "chapter": "Continuity and Differentiability",
          "topic": "Continuity at a point",
          "content_type": "worked_example",
          "text": "Let f(x) = (x²−1)/(x−1) for x≠1 and f(1)=2. For x≠1 the expression simplifies to x+1, whose limit at 1 is 2; this equals f(1), so f is continuous at 1.",
          "reference_id": "adapted-original-mathematics-12",
          "syllabus_reference_id": "cbse-2026-27-mathematics-041",
          "page_start": null,
          "page_end": null,
          "language": "en",
          "review_status": "teacher_review_required"
        },
        {
