          "topic": "Conditional probability and independence",
          "content_type": "explanation",
          "text": "Conditional probability is P(A|B)=P(A∩B)/P(B) when P(B)>0. Events A and B are independent when learning that B occurred does not change the probability of A; equivalently P(A∩B)=P(A)P(B).",
