          "topic": "Conditional probability and independence",
          "content_type": "worked_example",
          "text": "For a fair die, let A be “even” and B be “greater than 3.” Then A∩B={4,6}; P(A|B)=2/3, while P(A)=1/2, so these events are not independent.",
